[2026-03-14T19:15:03.206Z] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Hu9bD3eYPeNzcoQ6uu6RTw","type":"tool_result","content":"   500→\n   501→#### Test: Inbox page shows empty state when no notifications\n   502→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, has no notifications\n   503→- **Expected**: The page displays a friendly empty state message with an icon (e.g., \"No notifications yet\" or \"You're all caught up!\") instead of an empty list.\n   504→\n   505→#### Test: Inbox shows unread notifications visually distinct from read\n   506→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, has 2 unread notifications and 1 read notification\n   507→- **Expected**: Unread notifications appear with bold text and a left border accent (using the primary accent color `#5e6ad2`). Read notifications appear with normal weight text and no left border accent.\n   508→\n   509→#### Test: Inbox page shows notification count in header\n   510→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, has 5 unread notifications\n   511→- **Expected**: The inbox header or a badge near it indicates the number of unread notifications (e.g., \"Inbox (5)\" or a count badge).\n   512→\n   513→#### Test: Inbox notification list updates sidebar badge when notifications change\n   514→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, has 3 unread notifications, sidebar Inbox badge shows \"3\"\n   515→- **Action**: User marks one notification as read on the inbox page\n   516→- **Expected**: The sidebar Inbox badge updates to \"2\".\n   517→\n   518→#### Test: Inbox notifications are ordered by newest first\n   519→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, has notifications from 5 minutes ago, 1 hour ago, and 1 day ago\n   520→- **Expected**: Notifications appear in order: 5 minutes ago (top), 1 hour ago (middle), 1 day ago (bottom).\n   521→\n   522→#### Test: Archiving a notification removes it from the list\n   523→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, has 3 notifications visible in the inbox\n   524→- **Action**: User clicks the archive button/icon on the first notification\n   525→- **Expected**: The notification is removed from the inbox list. The list now shows 2 notifications. The archived notification does not reappear.\n   526→\n   527→#### Test: Archiving multiple notifications works in sequence\n   528→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, has 3 notifications visible\n   529→- **Action**: User archives the first notification, then archives what is now the first notification\n   530→- **Expected**: Both notifications are removed. The list shows 1 remaining notification. The archive action works correctly on repeated use.\n   531→\n   532→#### Test: All notifications can be archived to reach empty state\n   533→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, has 2 notifications visible\n   534→- **Action**: User archives both notifications one by one\n   535→- **Expected**: After all notifications are archived, the empty state message is displayed. The sidebar Inbox badge disappears (no unread count).\n   536→\n   537→### NotificationRow\n   538→\n   539→#### Test: Notification row displays assignment notification correctly\n   540→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, has a notification for \"Issue ENG-42 was assigned to you\" created 5 minutes ago\n   541→- **Expected**: The notification row displays: an assignment-type icon (e.g., user-plus or assign icon), issue identifier \"ENG-42\", description text \"assigned to you\" or similar, and relative timestamp \"5m ago\". The row is visually complete and well-formatted.\n   542→\n   543→#### Test: Notification row displays issue update notification correctly\n   544→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, has a notification for \"Issue ENG-15 status changed to Done\" on a subscribed issue, created 1 hour ago\n   545→- **Expected**: The notification row displays: an update-type icon (e.g., refresh or edit icon), issue identifier \"ENG-15\", description \"status changed to Done\" or similar, and relative timestamp \"1h ago\".\n   546→\n   547→#### Test: Notification row displays mention notification correctly\n   548→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, has a notification for \"You were mentioned in a comment on ENG-7\" created 2 hours ago\n   549→- **Expected**: The notification row displays: a mention-type icon (e.g., at-sign icon), issue identifier \"ENG-7\", description \"mentioned you in a comment\" or similar, and relative timestamp \"2h ago\".\n   550→\n   551→#### Test: Clicking an unread notification marks it as read\n   552→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, has an unread notification for issue ENG-42 (bold text, left border accent)\n   553→- **Action**: User clicks on the notification row\n   554→- **Expected**: The notification's visual style changes from unread (bold, left border accent) to read (normal weight, no left border accent). The change is persisted to the database. The sidebar Inbox badge count decrements by 1.\n   555→\n   556→#### Test: Clicking a read notification does not change its state\n   557→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, has a read notification (normal weight, no accent)\n   558→- **Action**: User clicks on the notification row\n   559→- **Expected**: The notification remains in its read visual state. No redundant database update is made.\n   560→\n   561→#### Test: Clicking a notification navigates to the related issue\n   562→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, has a notification for issue ENG-42\n   563→- **Action**: User clicks on the notification row\n   564→- **Expected**: User is navigated to `/issue/<issueId>` for issue ENG-42. The issue detail page loads showing ENG-42.\n   565→\n   566→#### Test: Notification row archive button is visible\n   567→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, has a notification visible in the inbox\n   568→- **Expected**: Each notification row has an archive button/icon (e.g., an archive or x icon) visible on hover or always visible, allowing the user to archive the notification.\n   569→\n   570→#### Test: Notification row archive button archives without navigating\n   571→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, viewing the inbox with a notification for ENG-42\n   572→- **Action**: User clicks the archive button on the ENG-42 notification row\n   573→- **Expected**: The notification is archived and removed from the list. The user remains on the `/inbox` page — no navigation to the issue detail occurs. The archive action is persisted to the database.\n   574→\n   575→#### Test: Notification row shows correct icon per notification type\n   576→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, has one of each notification type: assignment, issue update, mention\n   577→- **Expected**: Each notification type has a distinct, recognizable icon: assignment uses a user/assign icon, issue update uses a refresh/change icon, mention uses an at-sign/@-symbol icon. The icons are visually differentiated by shape or style.\n   578→\n   579→#### Test: Notification row displays relative timestamps that update\n   580→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, has a notification created \"just now\"\n   581→- **Expected**: The timestamp shows \"just now\" or \"1m ago\" (relative format). Timestamps use relative format throughout (e.g., \"5m ago\", \"1h ago\", \"2d ago\") rather than absolute dates.\n   582→\n   583→#### Test: Marking notification as read then archiving works correctly\n   584→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, has an unread notification for ENG-42\n   585→- **Action**: User clicks the notification to mark as read, then clicks the archive button on the same notification\n   586→- **Expected**: The notification is first marked as read (visual change), then archived and removed from the list. Both actions succeed in sequence without conflict.\n   587→\n   588→#### Test: Notification row click and archive button have separate hit targets\n   589→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, has a notification in the inbox\n   590→- **Action**: User clicks specifically on the archive button area of a notification row\n   591→- **Expected**: Only the archive action fires — the notification is archived. The user does NOT navigate to the issue detail page. The click targets for \"mark as read + navigate\" and \"archive\" are clearly separated.\n   592→\n   593→## Team Issues Page (`/team/:teamId/issues`)\n   594→\n   595→**Components**: TeamIssuesList, BulkActions, GroupBySort, TeamFilters\n   596→\n   597→### TeamIssuesList\n   598→\n   599→#### Test: Team Issues page renders with header showing team name\n   600→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, navigates to `/team/eng-1/issues` for team \"Engineering\"\n   601→- **Expected**: The page displays a header with the team name \"Engineering\" and an \"Issues\" label. A \"New Issue\" button is visible in the header area.\n   602→\n   603→#### Test: Team Issues page shows issues grouped by status (default)\n   604→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, \"Engineering\" team has issues in Backlog (3), In Progress (2), Done (1)\n   605→- **Expected**: Issues are grouped under status headers. Each group header shows the status icon, status name, and issue count in parentheses. Groups appear in status order: Backlog, Todo, In Progress, In Review, Done, Cancelled. Empty status groups are not displayed.\n   606→\n   607→#### Test: Team Issues page shows all team issues, not just current user's\n   608→- **Initial state**: User \"Alice\" is authenticated, \"Engineering\" team has issues: ENG-1 (assigned to Alice), ENG-2 (assigned to Bob), ENG-3 (unassigned)\n   609→- **Expected**: All three issues (ENG-1, ENG-2, ENG-3) are visible on the team issues page.\n   610→\n   611→#### Test: Team Issues page shows empty state when team has no issues\n   612→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, \"Engineering\" team has no issues\n   613→- **Expected**: A friendly empty state message with an icon is displayed (e.g., \"No issues yet. Create your first issue to get started.\") and the \"New Issue\" button is visible.\n   614→\n   615→#### Test: Issue row displays all required fields including checkbox and team prefix\n   616→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, viewing team issues. Issue ENG-42 exists with title \"Fix login bug\", status \"In Progress\", priority \"High\", labels [\"Bug\"], assignee \"Jane Doe\" (with avatar), due date \"2026-03-20\", project \"Auth Rewrite\".\n   617→- **Expected**: The issue row displays: a checkbox for bulk selection (unchecked), High priority icon (orange arrow-up), identifier \"ENG-42\" with team prefix, title \"Fix login bug\", In Progress status icon (yellow half circle), \"Bug\" label as a small colored badge, assignee avatar, due date \"Mar 20\", and project name \"Auth Rewrite\".\n   618→\n   619→#### Test: Issue row title is clickable and navigates to issue detail\n   620→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, viewing team issues with issue ENG-42\n   621→- **Action**: User clicks on the title \"Fix login bug\" in the issue row\n   622→- **Expected**: User is navigated to `/issue/<issueId>` for issue ENG-42.\n   623→\n   624→#### Test: Issue row status icon is clickable to change status\n   625→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, viewing team issues. Issue ENG-42 has status \"Todo\".\n   626→- **Action**: User clicks the status icon on the ENG-42 issue row\n   627→- **Expected**: A dropdown/popover appears showing all available statuses (Backlog, Todo, In Progress, In Review, Done, Cancelled) with their respective icons and colors.\n   628→\n   629→#### Test: Changing status via issue row status dropdown persists and moves issue between groups\n   630→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, viewing team issues grouped by status. \"Todo\" group has ENG-42. \"In Progress\" group has 1 issue.\n   631→- **Action**: User clicks the status icon on ENG-42, selects \"In Progress\" from the dropdown\n   632→- **Expected**: The dropdown closes. ENG-42 moves from the \"Todo\" group to the \"In Progress\" group. Group counts update accordingly. The change is persisted to the database.\n   633→\n   634→#### Test: Issue row status dropdown can be used multiple times\n   635→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, issue ENG-42 has status \"Todo\"\n   636→- **Action**: User clicks status icon, changes to \"In Progress\", then clicks status icon again, changes to \"Done\"\n   637→- **Expected**: Both status changes work correctly. The issue ends up in the \"Done\" group with a green check circle icon. Each dropdown opens and closes cleanly.\n   638→\n   639→#### Test: Status group headers are collapsible\n   640→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, \"In Progress\" group is expanded with 2 issues\n   641→- **Action**: User clicks the \"In Progress\" group header\n   642→- **Expected**: The group collapses, hiding all issues within it. The group header remains visible with a collapse indicator (e.g., chevron rotates). Clicking again expands the group back.\n   643→\n   644→#### Test: Status group collapse toggles multiple times\n   645→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, \"Backlog\" group is expanded with 3 issues\n   646→- **Action**: User clicks the \"Backlog\" header to collapse, clicks it again to expand, then collapses once more\n   647→- **Expected**: Each click toggles correctly. After three clicks, the group is collapsed and its issues are hidden. The count in parentheses remains accurate.\n   648→\n   649→#### Test: Multiple status groups can be independently collapsed\n   650→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, has issues in Backlog, In Progress, and Done groups, all expanded\n   651→- **Action**: User collapses the \"Backlog\" group, then collapses the \"Done\" group\n   652→- **Expected**: \"Backlog\" and \"Done\" groups are collapsed while \"In Progress\" remains expanded showing its issues.\n   653→\n   654→#### Test: Issue row displays priority icon with correct color\n   655→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, viewing team issues with issues at different priorities\n   656→- **Expected**: Urgent shows red alert-triangle icon, High shows orange arrow-up, Medium shows yellow minus, Low shows blue arrow-down, No Priority shows gray dots-horizontal.\n   657→\n   658→#### Test: Issue row displays labels as colored badges\n   659→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, issue ENG-42 has labels \"Bug\" (red) and \"Frontend\" (blue)\n   660→- **Expected**: Both labels are shown as small colored badges in the issue row, each with the label's color and name text.\n   661→\n   662→#### Test: Issue row shows assignee avatar\n   663→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, issue ENG-42 is assigned to \"Jane Doe\" who has an avatar\n   664→- **Expected**: The issue row shows Jane Doe's avatar as a small circular image. If no avatar, shows initials.\n   665→\n   666→#### Test: Issue row hides optional fields when not set\n   667→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, issue ENG-43 has no labels, no due date, no project, no assignee\n   668→- **Expected**: The issue row does not show empty placeholders for labels, due date, project, or assignee. Only the present fields (checkbox, priority, identifier, title, status) are shown.\n   669→\n   670→#### Test: New Issue button opens create issue modal with team pre-selected\n   671→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, viewing `/team/eng-1/issues` for team \"Engineering\"\n   672→- **Action**: User clicks the \"New Issue\" button\n   673→- **Expected**: The create issue modal opens with the team selector pre-set to \"Engineering\". The title field is focused.\n   674→\n   675→#### Test: New Issue button text and icon appearance\n   676→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, viewing team issues page\n   677→- **Expected**: The \"New Issue\" button is visible with text \"New Issue\" and displays appropriately (e.g., with a plus icon). The button uses the primary accent style.\n   678→\n   679→#### Test: Newly created issue appears in the list\n   680→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, viewing team issues for \"Engineering\" with 3 issues\n   681→- **Action**: User clicks \"New Issue\", fills in the title \"New feature request\" with status \"Backlog\", and submits the form\n   682→- **Expected**: The modal closes. The new issue appears in the \"Backlog\" group with the next sequential identifier (e.g., ENG-44). The group count updates.\n   683→\n   684→### BulkActions\n   685→\n   686→#### Test: Issue row checkboxes are visible and unchecked by default\n   687→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, viewing team issues with 5 issues\n   688→- **Expected**: Each issue row has a checkbox on the left side. All checkboxes are unchecked by default.\n   689→\n   690→#### Test: Clicking a checkbox selects an issue\n   691→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, viewing team issues with ENG-42 unchecked\n   692→- **Action**: User clicks the checkbox on ENG-42\n   693→- **Expected**: The checkbox becomes checked. The issue row has a selected visual style (e.g., highlighted background). A bulk action toolbar appears at the top or bottom of the list.\n   694→\n   695→#### Test: Clicking a checked checkbox deselects the issue\n   696→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, ENG-42 checkbox is checked, bulk action toolbar is visible\n   697→- **Action**: User clicks the checkbox on ENG-42 again\n   698→- **Expected**: The checkbox becomes unchecked. The selected visual style is removed from the row. If no other issues are selected, the bulk action toolbar disappears.\n   699→"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_017o3c7ZbXzUdsG6RF8aGt3H","session_id":"99814115-c30e-4f87-9cbf-74bddf769cac","uuid":"9a0933b4-f029-42b0-af68-5175a9020273"}
