nt from database\n  - Database queries: Looks for unread AND not archived notifications\n  - Pattern: Bearer token auth, session lookup, SQL query\n\n#### Store Configuration\n- `/repo/apps/LinearClone/src/store.ts` - Redux store with reducers already including notificationsReducer\n\n### Database Schema Details\nFrom `notifications-count.ts`, the notifications table has fields:\n- `member_id` - The user the notification is for\n- `read` - Boolean for read status\n- `archived` - Boolean for archived status\n- Expected fields (from test specs): type, issue info, description, created_at\n\n### Test Requirements\nKey test expectations from `/repo/apps/LinearClone/docs/tests.md` (lines 491-592):\n\n**NotificationList**:\n- Renders header \"Inbox\" with notification count (e.g., \"Inbox (5)\")\n- Lists notifications in reverse chronological order (newest first)\n- Empty state: \"No notifications yet\" or \"You're all caught up!\" message\n- Unread vs read styling: unread has bold text + left border accent (#5e6ad2)\n- Archive button removes notification from list\n- Sidebar badge updates when notifications change\n- Test data: 3 notification types - assignment, issue update, mention\n\n**NotificationRow**:\n- **Assignment**: icon (user-plus), identifier \"ENG-42\", text \"assigned to you\", timestamp \"5m ago\"\n- **Update**: icon (refresh/edit), identifier \"ENG-15\", text \"status changed to Done\", timestamp \"1h ago\"\n- **Mention**: icon (at-sign), identifier \"ENG-7\", text \"mentioned you in a comment\", timestamp \"2h ago\"\n- Click notification: marks as read, navigates to issue detail page\n- Archive button: removes from list WITHOUT navigating\n- Click targets must be separate (row vs archive button)\n- Timestamps use relative format with updates\n\n### Design System / Styling\n\n**Color Variables** (from existing CSS):\n- `--color-text-primary` - Primary text\n- `--color-text-secondary` - Secondary text\n- `--color-text-tertiary` - Tertiary/muted text\n- `--color-bg` - Main background\n- `--color-bg-surface` - Surface background (hover states)\n- `--color-bg-hover` - Hover background\n- `--color-border` - Border color\n- `--color-accent` - Primary accent (#5e6ad2 - Linear's purple-blue)\n\n**Component Patterns**:\n- Row height: 36px (compact)\n- Row layout: Flex with left/right sections\n- Hover effect: background-color transition 150ms ease\n- Empty states: Centered icon + text, padding 64px 24px\n- Typography: 14px medium for titles, 13px secondary, 12px tertiary, 11px badges\n- Spacing: 8px gaps between elements, 12px padding in rows\n\n**Status/Priority Icons**:\n- Defined in `IssueRow.tsx` as SVG components\n- Pattern: statusConfig and priorityConfig objects with label/color\n- Can follow similar pattern for notification type icons\n\n### Redux/State Management\n\n**Store structure**: RootState includes:\n```typescript\nauth: { token: string | null }\nnotifications: { unreadCount: number; loading: boolean }\nissues: { myIssues: Issue[]; loading: boolean; error: string | null }\n// ... other slices\n```\n\n**Issue type** (for reference):\n```typescript\ninterface Issue {\n  id: string; title: string; identifier: string;\n  status: string; priority: string; number: number;\n  assigneeId: string | null; assigneeName: string | null;\n  // ... + labels, dueDate, createdAt, updatedAt, etc.\n}\n```\n\n### Specification Details\nFrom `/repo/apps/LinearClone/AppSpec.md`:\n- Inbox page shows notifications for:\n  - Issue assigned to you\n  - Issue subscribed to was updated\n  - You were mentioned in a comment\n- Visual distinction: unread (bold + left border accent), read (normal)\n- Features: Mark as read (click), Archive (button), Navigate to issue\n- Sidebar shows Inbox with notification count badge\n\n### Files Not Yet Created\n- `/repo/apps/LinearClone/src/components/NotificationRow.tsx` - Needs to be created\n- `/repo/apps/LinearClone/src/components/NotificationRow.css` - Needs to be created\n- `/repo/apps/LinearClone/src/components/NotificationList.tsx` - Needs to be created\n- `/repo/apps/LinearClone/src/components/NotificationList.css` - Needs to be created\n- `/repo/apps/LinearClone/src/pages/Inbox.tsx` - Needs to be created\n- `/repo/apps/LinearClone/src/pages/Inbox.css` - Needs to be created\n- Possibly API endpoints for:\n  - `/api/notifications` - Fetch notifications list\n  - `/api/notifications/:id/read` - Mark notification as read\n  - `/api/notifications/:id/archive` - Archive notification\n\n### Additional Context from CLAUDE.md\nThe repository includes `CLAUDE.md` which references `AGENTS.md` - these contain agent building guidelines and task management protocols.\n\nThis comprehensive context is ready for implementation of the three Inbox-related components."},{"type":"text","text":"agentId: a6c4b7369bcb0403f (for resuming to continue this agent's work if needed)\n<usage>total_tokens: 60348\ntool_uses: 52\nduration_ms: 103930</usage>"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"99814115-c30e-4f87-9cbf-74bddf769cac","uuid":"b85c7f45-97ea-400c-ba7c-18882e90eb07","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"Find which app this is about. Look for:\n1. The app directory under /repo/apps/ - list all app directories\n2. Read the task file at /repo/tasks/ to find which app the current task is for\n3. Read the AppSpec.md for that app\n4. Read the docs/tests.md for that app\n5. Read any style guides (AppStyle.md at /repo/apps/ level and app-specific level)\n6. List the current src/components/ and src/pages/ directories to see what exists already\n7. Read the existing schema.ts to understand the database tables\n8. Read any existing Redux slices related to notifications or inbox\n\nBe thorough - I need all this context to write components.","agentId":"a6c4b7369bcb0403f","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! Now I have all the context I need. Let me create a comprehensive report:\n\n## Context Summary for LinearClone Inbox Implementation\n\nI've thoroughly explored 